kwDOAO6SJc6zuUzK","user":{"login":"Logharn","id":112166548,"node_id":"U_kgDOBq-GlA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112166548?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Logharn","html_url":"https://github.com/Logharn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Logharn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Logharn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Logharn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Logharn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Logharn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Logharn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Logharn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Logharn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Logharn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-28T13:30:09Z","updated_at":"2025-06-28T13:30:09Z","body":"Ok, but if I output simple maths, values are as expected.\nWhat happens inside the rotation property that makes PI not PI?\nMoreover how can I evaluate if a node is rotated by PI?\nBecause if in the _ready() I put:\n\nself.rotation = PI\nprint(self.rotation == PI)\n\nreturns false\n\nI've to transform radians in degrees and then round it to the nearest integer?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3015265482/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3015270410","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108071#issuecomment-3015270410","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108071","id":3015270410,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6zuWAK","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-28T13:35:24Z","updated_at":"2025-06-28T13:35:24Z","body":"You can use `is_equal_approx(self.rotation, PI)`, see the notes in the `float` documentation:\nhttps://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_float.html#description","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3015270410/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3015309905","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108071#issuecomment-3015309905","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108071","id":3015309905,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6zufpR","user":{"login":"timothyqiu","id":372476,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MjQ3Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/372476?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu","html_url":"https://github.com/timothyqiu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-28T14:09:38Z","updated_at":"2025-06-28T14:09:38Z","body":"I think it's fair to expect that `0 + x == x` even if `x` is a floating-point number.\n\nThe actual problem here is that `rotation` being 32-bit, while `PI` (a regular `float`) being 64-bit.\n\nWe could improve the documentation for special properties / parameters / return values like this. Otherwise, the only way to find out the reason is to check to source code for the use of `real_t`.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3015309905/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]